<!--
  ats_invalid_negative_total_ventas.xml — DESPITE THE FILE NAME, THIS DOCUMENT
  IS ACCEPTED. The file name records the intent of the case, not its verdict.

  Rule exercised: totalVentasType, ats.xsd:1298-1303. Its pattern at
  ats.xsd:1302 is
    "[0-9]{1,12}\.[0-9]{2}|[0-9]{1,12}|[\-][0-9]{1,12}\.[0-9]{2}|[\-][0-9]{1,12}"
  — the only amount type in the whole schema that carries the two negative
  alternatives. The type has no minInclusive at all, so "-1500.00" validates.

  Element under test: iva/totalVentas, ats.xsd:605-607.

  THIS IS WHERE THE SCHEMA IS NOT THE NORM, and it is the asymmetry that makes
  credit-note handling non-obvious: a negative totalVentas is legal while a
  negative per-line amount is not (compare ats_invalid_negative_line_amount.xml,
  where monedaType ats.xsd:1304-1310 sets minInclusive 0.0). The aggregate is
  netted by the SRI, the lines are not. A builder that negates line amounts to
  represent a credit note produces a file the schema rejects; a builder that
  emits the negative total without touching the lines produces one it accepts.
  Which of the two the SRI actually expects is a question for the business
  validators of the Validaciones column, not for the XSD.
-->
